# ShellCheck configuration for iArch by Safari.
#
# The CI gate is:
#     shellcheck --severity=warning -- $(git ls-files '*.sh')
# Errors and warnings must be zero. Info and style findings are visible when you
# run shellcheck locally but are deliberately not gating: several of them ask for
# quoting styles this repository's generated-configuration code cannot use.
#
# Exceptions are listed inline, next to the line they apply to, each with its
# reason in the same comment. Nothing is disabled repository-wide, because a
# global disable hides the finding in files that have not been written yet.
# The exceptions in use today:
#
#   SC2034  install.sh:541, fedora_install.sh:449, legacy/legacy-install.sh:444
#           Palette entries are defined as one table and only some are read by
#           the branch that follows; splitting the table would hide the pairing.
#   SC2317  lib/iarch-common.sh:27
#           The usage function is reached only when the library is executed
#           instead of sourced, which shellcheck cannot see from a sourced file.
#   SC2016  tests/session-install.sh:71
#   SC2088  tests/session-install.sh:73
#           The test asserts that a literal "$HOME" and a literal "~/..." string
#           appear in a generated file. Expanding them would test nothing.
#
# `shell` is stated here so files that are sourced rather than executed are still
# analysed as bash, and so a missing or unusual shebang cannot silently switch
# the dialect (POSIX sh would flag every bash array in this repository).
shell=bash
